# fixedbugs, defect 2364, lane p239-land-a, 2026-11-09 (panel 239's R4 and
# R5; the briefs' `own`).
#
# Module `mixes` reads its own `fixedbugs-2364-m.h` first, which defines the
# macro under which `fixedbugs-2364-rs.h` lays `Rs` out wide, and spells
# `rs.Rs`; module `rs` reads `rs.h` alone, narrow. A unit's own headers come
# first (panel 204's R1), so no order makes the two readings alike, and the
# program is refused before any unit compiles, told where `mixes` spells the
# record, the line its author can change. Before the repair it was refused
# with *`Rs.a` is `long long` in `rs.h`*, false of `rs.h` as module `rs`
# reads it, at `rs`'s correct field.
use fixedbugs2364/mixes
use fixedbugs2364/rs

function main()
    print(mixes.total(x: rs.make(v: 3)))
